<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="updated">Last updated: September 21, 2026</p>

<p>This Privacy Policy explains how the AI Job Recommendation System ("the Service")
collects, uses, stores, and protects information when you use the Service.</p>

<section><h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>Depending on the features you use, the Service may collect:</p>
<ul>
<li>Account information such as your name and email address.</li>
<li>Resume, profile, skills, preferences, and job-search information that you choose to provide.</li>
<li>Job, application, and application-status information associated with your use of the Service.</li>
<li>Information obtained from third-party platforms when you explicitly authorize an integration.</li>
<li>Technical information needed to operate, secure, and troubleshoot the Service.</li>
</ul></section>

<section><h2>2. LinkedIn and Third-Party Integrations</h2>
<p>If you connect a LinkedIn account, the Service uses LinkedIn's authorization mechanisms
and only requests permissions made available to the application and approved for its use.</p>
<p>Information received through an authorized integration is used only for functionality
described by the Service, such as account connection and supported job or application
workflows. We do not sell LinkedIn data or use it for unrelated purposes.</p></section>

<section><h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
<ul>
<li>Provide and personalize job and internship recommendations.</li>
<li>Analyze resumes and user-provided career information.</li>
<li>Support job discovery, application workflows, and application tracking.</li>
<li>Send service-related email or notification updates.</li>
<li>Maintain, secure, debug, and improve the Service.</li>
</ul></section>

<section><h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell personal information. Information may be processed by service providers
necessary to operate the Service, subject to appropriate safeguards. Information may also
be disclosed where required by law or to protect the security and integrity of the Service.</p>
</section>

<section><h2>5. OAuth Tokens and Security</h2>
<p>OAuth credentials and tokens used for connected services are stored using security
controls intended to protect them from unauthorized access. Access is limited to
functionality required to operate the authorized integration.</p>
<p>No security measure can guarantee absolute security, but we take reasonable technical
and organizational measures to protect data.</p></section>

<section><h2>6. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
<p>We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the Service,
comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, and maintain legitimate business records.</p>
<p>Users may request deletion of their account and associated personal information, subject
to applicable legal or operational requirements. Disconnecting a third-party integration
stops the Service from using that connection for future authorized operations.</p></section>

<section><h2>7. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>The Service may integrate with third-party platforms such as LinkedIn and other job
platforms. Their services are governed by their own privacy policies and terms. We are
not responsible for privacy practices of third parties outside the Service.</p></section>

<section><h2>8. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>The Service is not intended for children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
personal information from children under 13.</p></section>

<section><h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy when the Service, integrations, or applicable
requirements change. The updated version will be published on this page with a revised
"Last updated" date.</p></section>

<section><h2>10. Contact</h2>
<p>For privacy questions, data-access requests, or deletion requests, please contact
the Service administrator through the contact details provided with the Service.</p></section>
